  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accountable Local Governance Programme, Phase 2 in Mali</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen the social contract between actors through inclusive governance of local public affairs through training on decentralisation, good governance, conflict management, gender and social inclusion, capacity building of local authorities and advocacy for a better consideration of the needs of youth and women in the plans and budgets of their commune 2400 young people including 1200 women and 80 communal councils will be direct beneficiaries of the project in the 80 communes of the Mopti, Bandiagara and Douentza region.</narrative>
  </description>
